# The circuit toolchain, named in exactly one place.
#
# scripts/build.sh, scripts/install-toolchain.sh, the build-circuits workflow
# and ../scripts/generate_srs.sh read this file. Nothing else may spell these
# versions out -- three copies of a version is how they drift.
#
# The set is decided by the phone, not by what is newest: mopro-ffi 0.3.7's
# Noir template uses noir-rs NOIR_RS_TAG, which links barretenberg-rs
# =BB_VERSION and executes circuits compiled by NARGO_VERSION. A circuit, its
# verification key and its Solidity verifier must come from this same set or
# the phone produces proofs nothing else accepts. Changing any line means
# rebuilding every circuit, redeploying every verifier and rebuilding mopro.
#
# 1.0.0 / 6.0.0 (2026-11-17, user decision): Noir's first stable release and
# the bb that Aztec's bbup pairs with it. scripts/install-toolchain.sh puts
# them in versioned folders beside the previous set, and scripts/lib/toolchain.sh
# makes every repository script use those folders, never PATH.
NARGO_VERSION=1.0.0
BB_VERSION=6.0.0
# The phone's prover is the parent repository's mopro/vendor/noir-rs: upstream
# zkmopro/noir-rs v1.0.0-beta.19 (commit 0e4fdc9), vendored and ported to the
# Noir crates at tag v1.0.0 and barretenberg-rs =6.0.0 (its MANIFEST and
# PATCHES.md). zkmopro has published no tag for Noir 1.0.0, so this is a local
# label, not an upstream tag: it keys the .srs stamps build.sh writes and names
# the LocalSrs layout scripts/generate_srs.sh produces. ../scripts/mopro_build.sh
# refuses to build when the vendored copy's Noir tag is not v<NARGO_VERSION> or
# mopro/Cargo.lock's barretenberg-rs is not BB_VERSION. Change this label when
# that vendored copy changes.
NOIR_RS_TAG=vendored-0e4fdc9-noir-v1.0.0
